         value wins over the library's). The SDK's bundled regex only recognizes real
         telecom prefixes and rejects eSewa's own official test IDs (9711111111-14,
         prefix "971"), so it's relaxed here to any 10-digit number starting with 9. -->
    <string name="regex_mobile_number" translatable="false">^[9][0-9]{9}$</string>
